  "description": "High-performance .NET HTTP client. FastAutoClient auto-negotiates HTTP/1.1 + HTTP/2 + HTTP/3 per origin via TLS ALPN and Alt-Svc upgrades, with sticky-demote fallback when QUIC is blocked. FastFeatureClient layers an opt-in handler pipeline (decompression, cookies, redirects, retries, response cache, NDJSON, telemetry) over any IFastTransport. The four explicit transport clients (FastClient/FastH2Client/FastH3Client/FastAutoClient) all implement IFastTransport — pin a protocol when you need to (gRPC = H/2), or compose for everything else. Span-based codecs on arena buffers, per-core sharded H/1.1 pool, multiplexed H/2 connections, QUIC-multiplexed H/3 with QPACK dynamic table — beats System.Net.Http.HttpClient on latency and allocation. Includes CosmoWebSocket and gRPC framing primitives.",
